{{!
    @template theme_epure/read_aloud_bar

    The bar of the reading aloud (theme_epure/read_aloud), at the bottom of the screen: read (or pause, resume), stop,
    the speed, and the status said to the screen readers. The script changes the button « Read » as the reading goes.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * title - Name of the bar.
    * play - Text of the button that starts the reading.
    * stop - Text of the button that stops it.
    * rate - Label of the speed.
    * rates - Speeds: value, label, selected.

    Example context (json):
    {
        "title": "Reading aloud",
        "play": "Read",
        "stop": "Stop",
        "rate": "Speed",
        "rates": [{"value": 0.75, "label": "0.75"}, {"value": 1, "label": "1", "selected": true}]
    }
}}
<div class="epure-a11y-speechbar d-print-none" role="region" aria-label="{{title}}">
    <button type="button" class="btn btn-primary" data-action="play"><i class="fa fa-play" aria-hidden="true"></i> <span>{{play}}</span></button>
    <button type="button" class="btn btn-secondary" data-action="stop"><i class="fa fa-stop" aria-hidden="true"></i> <span>{{stop}}</span></button>
    <label class="epure-a11y-speechrate"><span>{{rate}}</span>
        <select class="form-select custom-select">
            {{#rates}}
            <option value="{{value}}"{{#selected}} selected{{/selected}}>{{label}} ×</option>
            {{/rates}}
        </select>
    </label>
    <p class="epure-a11y-speechstatus" role="status" data-region="status" hidden></p>
</div>
